# Normalizes line endings to LF in the repository and working tree,
# regardless of a clone's local core.autocrlf setting — matching
# .editorconfig's `end_of_line = lf`. Without this, Windows checkouts with
# autocrlf=true keep re-introducing CRLF, and the next `dotnet format` (or
# any other LF-respecting tool) flips it back, producing line-ending-only
# diffs on files nobody actually edited.
* text=auto eol=lf
